# App Python

Window and widgets do layout and signal wiring only. Carla I/O belongs in `services/` (`PatchController`, `CarlaOsc`, `MidiService`). MIDI record and loop playback stay in `services/midi/` and `PatchController`, not the UI.

# Rack / MIDI

- Split voice = same patch at `carla_idx + split_start_idx`. Indexes live in `main.py` `AppConfig`; do not invent new ones.
- Pigments (`preset_over_midi`): MIDI program change on channels 2 (main) / 3 (split) after `MIDI_PC_DELAY_MS`.
- Everything else: Carla OSC `/set_program`.
- Channel 1 is the keyboard; 16 is playback.

Comment *why*, not the next line. Good targets: Carla param/rack indexes, MIDI program-change delays, touch `NoFocus`, stacked main vs split grids. Skip narration like “create a button”.

```python
# ❌ BAD
self.midi.send_program_change(preset.idx, channel)  # send the program change

# ✅ GOOD
# Channels 2/3: midichanfilter in front of each Pigments (1 is keyboard).
self.midi.send_program_change(preset.idx, channel)
```
